  "summary": "Investigated the dashboard rendering pipeline end-to-end (server/api.go groupFeaturesByStage, board_fragment template in index.html, CSS, JS polling logic, and client-side state push in server_client.py). Found a likely root cause: the initial page render at '/' does NOT include 'ActiveSlugs' in the template data map (lines 252-258 of api.go), but the board_fragment template references '{{if index $.ActiveSlugs .Slug}}' (line 921 of index.html). In Go's template engine, calling 'index' on a nil map value causes a template execution error ('index of untyped nil'), which aborts rendering mid-stream. Since 'ideas' is the first stage in stageOrder, and html/template writes output directly to the ResponseWriter, the template crashes while rendering the first feature card in the ideas stage — resulting in only the ideas stage (partially) being visible, with all subsequent stages never rendered. The /api/board polling endpoint (lines 396-431) correctly includes ActiveSlugs and would fix the display after ~5 seconds, but the initial page load is broken. Fix: add 'ActiveSlugs' to the initial page render data map, computing it the same way as in /api/board (lines 412-420). Secondary observation: even without this bug, empty stages are collapsed by default (stage-body.hidden + stage-toggle.collapsed CSS classes), which could make the dashboard appear to 'only show ideas' if that's the only stage with items — consider making all stages visible by default or at least not collapsed."
